    <p>The 28 October post also cites internal secure-code tests, the Chrome team, and Wiz. Those have no shared test and stay off this card [5].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>As of 10 November 2026, Google says [1][2][3]:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Paying developers: build with the Gemini API paid tier in AI Studio and Android Studio. Google AI Ultra subscribers can also try it in Google Antigravity and AI Studio [1].</li>
      <li>Enterprises: try it in Gemini for business via the API or model drop down, Google Antigravity, or CodeMender [1].</li>
      <li>Everyday users: try Carbon starting today in the Gemini app and AI Mode in Search if they are Google AI Ultra subscribers [1]. The mid-post sentence also says access is “rolling out to all Google AI Ultra subscribers” in Antigravity, the Gemini app, and AI Mode in Search [1].</li>
      <li>Scientists and researchers: may apply for a chance to get Argon and Carbon via Google Antigravity’s highest usage tier free of charge for 6 months, onboarded on a rolling basis, subject to eligibility, capacity, and selection [1].</li>
      <li>Cybersecurity defenders: may “Apply to join the Fairwind Program to get access to Carbon for cyber on a rolling basis” [1].</li>
    </ul>
