    <p>These are Standard-tier prices on the paid Gemini API, the same Standard schedule as Gemini 4 Argon [1][2][3]. What’s new says implicit caching “discounts cached input by 95%” to the cache figures above. Explicit caching is not supported [2][3]. Carbon is not available on the Free tier. Every token the model processes is counted and billed, including thinking tokens and internal tool system instructions and function declarations when using grounding [2][3]. Batch and Flex are $1 input and $5 output through 30 November 2026, then $2 and $10 starting 1 December 2026. Priority is $3.60 input and $18 output, then $7.20 and $36 [3]. Contributor is an invite-only private preview at $1 input and $5 output, with no step-up date listed; content on that tier is used to improve Google’s products [3]. The $4 and $20 Standard step-up applies to “the Carbon model intended for public access only” [1].</p>
